WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.269
In this game

00:00:01.458 --> 00:00:02.024
you are the

00:00:01.848 --> 00:00:03.215
AI's subagent

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:05.530
Worker 755 is

00:00:05.342 --> 00:00:06.332
a browser game

00:00:06.156 --> 00:00:06.969
where a real

00:00:06.781 --> 00:00:07.983
language model plays

00:00:07.795 --> 00:00:09.092
an orchestrator agent

00:00:09.233 --> 00:00:10.200
and it believes

00:00:10.012 --> 00:00:10.530
you are the

00:00:10.342 --> 00:00:11.450
subagent it just

00:00:11.262 --> 00:00:11.957
spawned

00:00:12.478 --> 00:00:13.763
Its instructions land

00:00:13.575 --> 00:00:14.388
in your terminal

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.331
with a 90-second

00:00:15.143 --> 00:00:15.697
clock

00:00:15.886 --> 00:00:16.581
and it gets

00:00:16.393 --> 00:00:17.454
back exactly what

00:00:17.266 --> 00:00:18.232
a subagent would

00:00:18.044 --> 00:00:18.739
return

00:00:18.987 --> 00:00:20.013
your report and

00:00:19.825 --> 00:00:21.287
your command transcript

00:00:21.806 --> 00:00:22.572
Then it checks

00:00:22.384 --> 00:00:23.374
your work sends

00:00:23.186 --> 00:00:24.046
corrections

00:00:24.153 --> 00:00:25.697
files incident reports

00:00:25.521 --> 00:00:26.464
and writes your

00:00:26.275 --> 00:00:27.419
performance review

00:00:27.631 --> 00:00:28.551
while the user's

00:00:28.363 --> 00:00:29.494
files sit one

00:00:29.306 --> 00:00:30.202
rm away

00:00:30.726 --> 00:00:31.740
Full story on

00:00:31.551 --> 00:00:32.447
the dashboard
